    {
      "key": "barriers.html::node-188",
      "source": "SafeLearning/barriers.html",
      "locator": "::node-188",
      "line": 148,
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "source_text": "Barrier functions verify a closed loop; control barrier functions let us design one, exactly as Sontag's control Lyapunov functions extend Lyapunov functions. Take the control-affine system $\\dot x=f(x)+g(x)u$ with $f,g$ locally Lipschitz, $x\\in D\\subset\\mathbb R^n$, $u\\in U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^m$. Along any trajectory\n    $$\\dot h(x,u)=L_fh(x)+L_gh(x)\\,u,$$\n    which is affine in $u$. This single fact is why CBF conditions become linear constraints and safety filters become quadratic programs.",
      "text_sha256": "2c55185a17cf6d78d6d8172dbfab647ee62214ca5b4a218732dc1e4bb7a385b8",
